WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.940
Hi, I'm Nei Maldaner,

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.760
and this is module two of

3
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:04.460
OSWork.

4
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.400
In module one,

5
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.860
you learned to see AI as a

6
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.160
system of parts

7
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.020
and to delegate with limits.

8
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.700
Now we'll look at the places where

9
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:12.980
that work happens:

10
00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.480
the chat, Work,

11
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.573
and Desktop.

12
00:00:15.573 --> 00:00:17.420
You'll learn to recognize when a short

13
00:00:17.420 --> 00:00:18.820
question is enough,

14
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.280
turn a vague request into a work

15
00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.180
order with a clear finish,

16
00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.920
confirm what the AI actually read,

17
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.680
know where the task runs,

18
00:00:26.680 --> 00:00:27.680
write a delivery contract,

19
00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.000
and check what you got back.

20
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.800
There's no terminal in this module,

21
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.200
and the practices work in the chat

22
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:35.900
you already use or in a notepad,

23
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.040
even without Work or Desktop on your

24
00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.200
account.

25
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.260
Denise and Lúcia are still with us.

26
00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.060
When I ask,

27
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.620
pause the video and do the practice

28
00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:44.540
right then.

29
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.220
Not every task calls for a big

30
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.080
tool.

31
00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.200
Setting up a complicated routine for something

32
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.480
that only needed an answer wastes time

33
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.600
and gives you more to check.

34
00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.240
The chat is a conversation interface.

35
00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.260
Think of the question you ask a

36
00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:59.400
colleague in the hallway between classes:

37
00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.900
it's short, the answer comes right away,

38
00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:03.060
and you decide what to do with

39
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:03.660
it.

40
00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:04.900
If the answer doesn't work,

41
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.060
you don't start over,

42
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.340
you send an adjustment in the same

43
00:01:07.340 --> 00:01:08.520
conversation.

44
00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:10.160
Lúcia was covering a colleague's math class

45
00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.860
and asked for three ways to explain

46
00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:12.820
fractions using

47
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:14.800
the ingredients of a cake recipe.

48
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:16.480
She got half a cup of sugar,

49
00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.800
a quarter stick of butter,

50
00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:18.660
and a third of a cup of

51
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:19.340
milk.

52
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.840
She asked to swap the third one

53
00:01:20.840 --> 00:01:24.040
for three eggs split between two recipes,

54
00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:25.500
and got it:

55
00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.620
one and a half eggs each.

56
00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:28.600
That's the chat:

57
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.120
question, answer, and adjustment.

58
00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:34.080
A loose question gets an encyclopedia answer.

59
00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:35.340
When you say who will read it

60
00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:37.480
and what they'll do with the text,

61
00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.960
the answer comes out at the right

62
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.380
length and in the right tone.

63
00:01:41.580 --> 00:01:44.160
Denise needed to explain the class council

64
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:45.720
to the parents of sixth graders.

65
00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.520
She just asked what a class council

66
00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:49.720
is,

67
00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.680
and got a technical paragraph,

68
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:52.720
correct,

69
00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.900
but far too long for a note.

70
00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.660
Then she asked for the explanation in

71
00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.040
two sentences,

72
00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.480
for sixth-grade parents,

73
00:01:59.480 --> 00:02:01.035
because it was going in a note

74
00:02:01.035 --> 00:02:01.655
home.

75
00:02:01.655 --> 00:02:03.635
She got two simple sentences:

76
00:02:03.635 --> 00:02:05.135
the class council is a meeting of

77
00:02:05.135 --> 00:02:07.415
the teachers with the coordinators to talk

78
00:02:07.415 --> 00:02:09.215
about how each class and each student

79
00:02:09.215 --> 00:02:10.315
is doing,

80
00:02:10.315 --> 00:02:12.735
and it produces agreements to help whoever

81
00:02:12.735 --> 00:02:13.675
needs it.

82
00:02:13.675 --> 00:02:15.555
Same subject, now

83
00:02:15.735 --> 00:02:17.775
at the length and in the tone

84
00:02:17.775 --> 00:02:19.015
of the note.

85
00:02:19.015 --> 00:02:21.635
Every short question leaves gaps,

86
00:02:21.635 --> 00:02:24.335
and the AI fills those gaps without

87
00:02:24.335 --> 00:02:25.615
telling you:

88
00:02:25.615 --> 00:02:27.635
it assumes the age of the class,

89
00:02:27.635 --> 00:02:29.575
the tone, the length.

90
00:02:29.575 --> 00:02:31.755
That's why you ask it to list

91
00:02:31.755 --> 00:02:33.115
what it assumed.

92
00:02:33.115 --> 00:02:35.595
Lúcia asked for an opening question for

93
00:02:35.595 --> 00:02:37.275
her lesson on mixtures,

94
00:02:37.275 --> 00:02:39.235
and the list of assumptions showed the

95
00:02:39.235 --> 00:02:42.015
AI had pictured high school students.

96
00:02:42.255 --> 00:02:44.015
She corrected it in one line,

97
00:02:44.015 --> 00:02:45.895
the class is eighth grade,

98
00:02:45.895 --> 00:02:47.595
and the question was adjusted.

99
00:02:47.595 --> 00:02:50.175
So when is the chat enough?

100
00:02:50.175 --> 00:02:52.035
If what you need is an answer

101
00:02:52.035 --> 00:02:54.575
you read and check on the spot,

102
00:02:54.575 --> 00:02:55.915
the chat handles it.

103
00:02:55.915 --> 00:02:58.215
If it's a document with several sources,

104
00:02:58.215 --> 00:02:59.395
a conversation falls short.

105
00:02:59.395 --> 00:03:01.455
Pause the video now and use this

106
00:03:01.455 --> 00:03:03.155
template with a real question from this

107
00:03:03.155 --> 00:03:05.495
week, with no student names.

108
00:03:05.495 --> 00:03:07.715
Read the list of assumptions first and

109
00:03:07.715 --> 00:03:09.355
correct one of them in a short

110
00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:09.935
message.

111
00:03:09.935 --> 00:03:11.715
And when the task doesn't fit in

112
00:03:11.715 --> 00:03:12.495
a conversation?

113
00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:14.915
A job with several sources needs a

114
00:03:14.915 --> 00:03:16.715
definition of done.

115
00:03:16.775 --> 00:03:18.595
Without one, the AI may keep researching

116
00:03:18.595 --> 00:03:20.115
when you only needed to compare three

117
00:03:20.115 --> 00:03:21.875
options, and you get back a long

118
00:03:21.875 --> 00:03:23.155
text you don't know where to start

119
00:03:23.155 --> 00:03:23.655
reviewing.

120
00:03:23.595 --> 00:03:25.855
In Work, you don't talk sentence by

121
00:03:25.855 --> 00:03:26.355
sentence.

122
00:03:26.355 --> 00:03:27.655
You hand over a task,

123
00:03:27.655 --> 00:03:29.595
like an analysis or a document,

124
00:03:29.595 --> 00:03:31.015
and get the result back to review.

125
00:03:31.015 --> 00:03:32.795
Think of ordering a cake from a

126
00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:33.895
bakery:

127
00:03:33.895 --> 00:03:35.375
you say the flavor,

128
00:03:35.375 --> 00:03:36.615
the size, and the day,

129
00:03:36.615 --> 00:03:38.575
and you don't stand there watching the

130
00:03:38.575 --> 00:03:39.275
oven.

131
00:03:39.275 --> 00:03:40.835
An important note:

132
00:03:40.835 --> 00:03:43.775
Work isn't available on every plan.

133
00:03:43.775 --> 00:03:45.535
If you can't find it on yours,

134
00:03:45.535 --> 00:03:46.995
place the work order in the regular

135
00:03:46.995 --> 00:03:49.115
chat, and it works the same way.

136
00:03:49.115 --> 00:03:51.115
What changes is the request,

137
00:03:51.115 --> 00:03:52.255
not the tool.

138
00:03:52.255 --> 00:03:54.255
Denise had to hire the bus for

139
00:03:54.255 --> 00:03:55.555
the museum field trip,

140
00:03:55.555 --> 00:03:57.955
and she had three quotes to compare

141
00:03:57.955 --> 00:03:59.475
and bring to the principal.

142
00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:02.260
A work order says five things.

143
00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:04.260
The goal, which is what the result

144
00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.280
is for.

145
00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.480
The inputs, the material the AI can

146
00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.340
use.

147
00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:10.280
The output, the format of what comes

148
00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:11.140
back.

149
00:04:11.140 --> 00:04:13.200
The limits, what it shouldn't do.

150
00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.180
And the stop,

151
00:04:14.180 --> 00:04:15.620
when the work is over.

152
00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.780
It looks like the authorization from lesson

153
00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:19.660
six, and it's related:

154
00:04:19.740 --> 00:04:21.600
the authorization says what the AI can

155
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.720
do, and the work order says what

156
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.040
must exist at the end.

157
00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.440
Denise wrote the one for the bus

158
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:27.240
in five lines,

159
00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.700
in three minutes.

160
00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:30.380
She got back a

161
00:04:30.380 --> 00:04:32.220
three-row table, with

162
00:04:32.220 --> 00:04:34.120
only what was in the quotes.

163
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:35.920
And where a quote said nothing,

164
00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:38.180
it showed not informed instead of a

165
00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:38.920
guess.

166
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:41.180
That means the document doesn't cover it,

167
00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.580
not that the risk is zero.

168
00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:45.920
The fifth part deserves attention.

169
00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:47.120
Without a stop,

170
00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.600
the AI decides on its own when

171
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.900
it's done.

172
00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:51.100
Sometimes it stops early,

173
00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.240
but often it goes way too far.

174
00:04:53.240 --> 00:04:55.700
Lúcia asked for a comparison of microscope

175
00:04:55.700 --> 00:04:56.900
kits for the lab,

176
00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:57.740
just like that,

177
00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.580
with no limit,

178
00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:00.420
and got five pages,

179
00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:02.340
with kits from stores she'd never heard

180
00:05:02.340 --> 00:05:02.980
of.

181
00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:05.420
Then she limited it to three kits,

182
00:05:05.460 --> 00:05:07.300
to the catalogs she pasted,

183
00:05:07.300 --> 00:05:08.660
and to one table,

184
00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:11.060
with deliver and stop at the end.

185
00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:12.240
She got one page,

186
00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:13.980
three rows, ready to check,

187
00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:15.760
all from the material she provided.

188
00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:16.860
Pause the video now.

189
00:05:16.860 --> 00:05:18.380
Pick a research task you'd do this

190
00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:21.520
week, gather three fictional or public options,

191
00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.520
and fill in the five parts.

192
00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:24.460
Send it in Work,

193
00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:25.920
if your account has it,

194
00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.380
or in the regular chat.

195
00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.380
Check that only your options came back,

196
00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:31.420
in the format you asked for,

197
00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.360
with not informed wherever data was missing.

198
00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.740
The work order mentions files.

199
00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:38.400
But can the AI really read each

200
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.320
one?

201
00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:42.000
Many task failures are access failures.

202
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.320
You imagine

203
00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.320
the AI can see a folder that

204
00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:46.960
was never shared,

205
00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.660
and the answer talks about documents the

206
00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:50.100
model didn't read.

207
00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:51.820
Desktop is the app that lives on

208
00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:52.700
your computer.

209
00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:54.300
If your app offers it,

210
00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.380
it can open folders and other apps,

211
00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:58.160
always with your permission.

212
00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.935
But having the app doesn't give it

213
00:05:59.935 --> 00:06:02.035
access to all your documents.

214
00:06:02.035 --> 00:06:02.835
In the browser chat,

215
00:06:02.835 --> 00:06:05.505
you attach or paste each file.

216
00:06:05.505 --> 00:06:07.795
They're different paths with the same rule:

217
00:06:07.795 --> 00:06:10.655
the AI only reads what reached it.

218
00:06:10.935 --> 00:06:12.795
Lúcia uses the browser chat on the

219
00:06:12.795 --> 00:06:14.955
school computer and Desktop on her laptop

220
00:06:14.955 --> 00:06:17.335
at home, and in both she checks

221
00:06:17.335 --> 00:06:19.515
what the AI received before asking for

222
00:06:19.515 --> 00:06:20.215
the work.

223
00:06:20.215 --> 00:06:22.215
Giving access is like handing over the

224
00:06:22.215 --> 00:06:23.695
key to one drawer,

225
00:06:23.695 --> 00:06:25.235
not to the whole school.

226
00:06:25.235 --> 00:06:26.855
Put only what the task needs in

227
00:06:26.855 --> 00:06:28.075
a subfolder,

228
00:06:28.075 --> 00:06:30.255
and when the app asks for access,

229
00:06:30.255 --> 00:06:32.115
choose just that subfolder.

230
00:06:32.235 --> 00:06:34.355
Screen names change between versions.

231
00:06:34.355 --> 00:06:36.755
What doesn't change is choosing the smallest

232
00:06:36.755 --> 00:06:38.315
folder possible.

233
00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:41.315
Denise's science fair folder had three versions

234
00:06:41.315 --> 00:06:42.335
of the budget,

235
00:06:42.335 --> 00:06:43.695
and she wanted to test the AI

236
00:06:43.695 --> 00:06:46.115
without risking the original.

237
00:06:46.215 --> 00:06:48.275
She allowed only a subfolder of samples,

238
00:06:48.275 --> 00:06:49.875
with two copies.

239
00:06:49.875 --> 00:06:51.215
Before the comparison,

240
00:06:51.215 --> 00:06:52.535
she asked for the list of files

241
00:06:52.535 --> 00:06:54.275
the AI could read,

242
00:06:54.275 --> 00:06:55.655
with the first and last line of

243
00:06:55.655 --> 00:06:56.855
each one.

244
00:06:56.855 --> 00:06:58.275
A name alone doesn't prove it was

245
00:06:58.275 --> 00:06:59.015
read.

246
00:06:59.015 --> 00:07:00.455
The first and last line show that

247
00:07:00.455 --> 00:07:02.235
the beginning and the end came through,

248
00:07:02.235 --> 00:07:04.675
and you check them against the file.

249
00:07:04.675 --> 00:07:05.855
If the list is wrong,

250
00:07:05.855 --> 00:07:07.215
the problem is access,

251
00:07:07.215 --> 00:07:08.935
not the request.

252
00:07:08.935 --> 00:07:10.275
And what if Desktop isn't on your

253
00:07:10.275 --> 00:07:13.235
account, or can't reach the folder?

254
00:07:13.235 --> 00:07:15.415
Deliver the files a way that works.

255
00:07:15.495 --> 00:07:16.555
Attach them in the chat,

256
00:07:16.555 --> 00:07:18.155
with the button next to the message

257
00:07:18.155 --> 00:07:20.195
box, or paste the text with a

258
00:07:20.195 --> 00:07:21.775
header that has the file name on

259
00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:22.275
top.

260
00:07:21.775 --> 00:07:24.175
That's what Lúcia did with the procedure

261
00:07:24.175 --> 00:07:26.175
for a water and oil experiment and

262
00:07:26.175 --> 00:07:27.335
the materials list.

263
00:07:27.335 --> 00:07:29.455
She asked for the list before the

264
00:07:29.455 --> 00:07:31.455
summary, and the AI gave back both

265
00:07:31.455 --> 00:07:33.635
names with the right first and last

266
00:07:33.635 --> 00:07:34.135
lines.

267
00:07:33.895 --> 00:07:35.655
Pause the video and set up your

268
00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:37.215
practice folder.

269
00:07:37.855 --> 00:07:39.355
In Documents,

270
00:07:39.355 --> 00:07:40.475
create the folder treino-ia,

271
00:07:40.475 --> 00:07:41.675
with

272
00:07:42.735 --> 00:07:44.475
two text files,

273
00:07:44.475 --> 00:07:45.685
aviso-a and

274
00:07:45.685 --> 00:07:48.235
aviso-b, with three made-up lines each.

275
00:07:48.235 --> 00:07:50.095
Attach or paste them in the chat

276
00:07:50.095 --> 00:07:52.295
and ask for the list,

277
00:07:52.295 --> 00:07:53.425
without summarizing

278
00:07:53.425 --> 00:07:53.925
yet.

279
00:07:53.835 --> 00:07:55.275
Check names and lines.

280
00:07:55.275 --> 00:07:56.435
If something's wrong,

281
00:07:56.435 --> 00:07:57.715
send them again and ask for the

282
00:07:57.715 --> 00:07:58.389
list again.

283
00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.460
The file was read.

284
00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.720
But where does the work happen,

285
00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:04.160
and what happens if you close your

286
00:08:04.160 --> 00:08:05.340
laptop?

287
00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:07.020
A task doesn't keep going just because

288
00:08:07.020 --> 00:08:09.220
it started on a modern screen.

289
00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.360
If you don't know where it runs,

290
00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:11.900
you don't know why it stopped,

291
00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.860
or where to look for the result.

292
00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:15.040
In local execution,

293
00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.920
the work runs on your machine.

294
00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:18.160
It's like a cake in your oven

295
00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:20.260
at home: if the power goes out,

296
00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:21.520
the oven stops.

297
00:08:21.520 --> 00:08:24.440
Power, network, and your computer's permissions all

298
00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.640
matter.

299
00:08:26.180 --> 00:08:28.260
Lúcia asked Desktop to review the lesson

300
00:08:28.260 --> 00:08:31.220
plans that only exist on her laptop.

301
00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.320
The task ran on the laptop,

302
00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:34.840
read the folder with the term's lesson

303
00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.440
plans, and saved to that same folder.

304
00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.580
At six in the evening,

305
00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:40.720
she closed the lid and went home.

306
00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:41.600
The next day,

307
00:08:41.600 --> 00:08:44.300
the review had stopped halfway through.

308
00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:45.800
In the cloud,

309
00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:48.180
the work runs on remote computers.

310
00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:49.500
It's like the bakery:

311
00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.280
the oven doesn't depend on your house,

312
00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.840
but the baker only has the ingredients

313
00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:53.780
you brought.

314
00:08:53.780 --> 00:08:55.100
The chat you already use is an

315
00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:55.600
example.

316
00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.820
The model works on the company's computers,

317
00:08:57.820 --> 00:08:59.833
and that's why it only knows what

318
00:08:59.833 --> 00:09:01.753
you pasted or attached.

319
00:09:01.813 --> 00:09:03.393
Denise wants the draft of the attendance

320
00:09:03.393 --> 00:09:05.173
report to be ready even if she

321
00:09:05.173 --> 00:09:06.573
turns off her laptop.

322
00:09:06.573 --> 00:09:08.253
For that, the spreadsheet needs to be

323
00:09:08.253 --> 00:09:09.853
somewhere the cloud can reach.

324
00:09:09.853 --> 00:09:11.653
Neither one is better.

325
00:09:12.153 --> 00:09:14.013
Local depends on your computer being on,

326
00:09:14.013 --> 00:09:15.473
with network,

327
00:09:15.473 --> 00:09:16.893
and it reads the folders on your

328
00:09:16.893 --> 00:09:18.253
machine that you allow.

329
00:09:18.253 --> 00:09:19.993
The cloud depends on the tool and

330
00:09:19.993 --> 00:09:21.033
your plan,

331
00:09:21.033 --> 00:09:22.713
and it only reads the files sent

332
00:09:22.713 --> 00:09:24.873
or connected to it.

333
00:09:24.873 --> 00:09:26.893
Each one has a dependency you need

334
00:09:26.893 --> 00:09:27.433
to know.

335
00:09:27.433 --> 00:09:29.153
Watch out for a common assumption:

336
00:09:29.153 --> 00:09:30.913
I started it in Work,

337
00:09:30.913 --> 00:09:32.473
so it runs on its own.

338
00:09:32.473 --> 00:09:35.113
Some environments keep going without your machine

339
00:09:35.113 --> 00:09:37.553
on, but that depends on the feature,

340
00:09:37.553 --> 00:09:39.093
not on the name of the screen.

341
00:09:39.093 --> 00:09:40.453
When in doubt,

342
00:09:40.453 --> 00:09:41.733
look it up on the tool's help

343
00:09:41.733 --> 00:09:43.453
page, or test it:

344
00:09:43.453 --> 00:09:45.033
start a short task,

345
00:09:45.033 --> 00:09:46.373
close your laptop for ten minutes,

346
00:09:46.373 --> 00:09:48.453
and see if it moved forward.

347
00:09:48.453 --> 00:09:50.953
Denise wrote down on the project sheet,

348
00:09:50.953 --> 00:09:52.153
created

349
00:09:52.513 --> 00:09:53.353
in lesson five,

350
00:09:53.353 --> 00:09:55.433
where the report runs,

351
00:09:55.433 --> 00:09:56.153
where it reads from,

352
00:09:56.153 --> 00:09:57.933
and where it saves.

353
00:09:57.933 --> 00:09:59.627
And she wrote a pending item:

354
00:09:59.627 --> 00:10:01.307
she doesn't know how long the draft

355
00:10:01.307 --> 00:10:03.507
stays stored in the task.

356
00:10:03.507 --> 00:10:06.137
With that, she went to ask the

357
00:10:06.137 --> 00:10:07.687
school's support team.

358
00:10:07.687 --> 00:10:09.387
Pause the video and do the same

359
00:10:09.387 --> 00:10:10.567
for one of your tasks,

360
00:10:10.567 --> 00:10:13.487
on the sheet or in a notepad.

361
00:10:13.487 --> 00:10:15.527
Whatever you don't know becomes a pending

362
00:10:15.527 --> 00:10:17.927
item, along with where you'll look for

363
00:10:17.927 --> 00:10:18.667
the answer.

364
00:10:18.667 --> 00:10:20.727
Now let's bring the request,

365
00:10:20.727 --> 00:10:22.787
the files, and the check together in

366
00:10:22.787 --> 00:10:24.247
a single text,

367
00:10:24.347 --> 00:10:26.247
the delivery contract.

368
00:10:26.367 --> 00:10:27.487
Think of the work order at a

369
00:10:27.487 --> 00:10:28.407
repair shop.

370
00:10:28.407 --> 00:10:29.907
It has fixed fields:

371
00:10:29.907 --> 00:10:31.827
the device, the problem,

372
00:10:31.827 --> 00:10:32.747
what not to touch,

373
00:10:32.747 --> 00:10:34.987
and how to test it at pickup.

374
00:10:34.987 --> 00:10:37.487
Nobody writes fix it well.

375
00:10:37.787 --> 00:10:39.787
The delivery contract is the work order

376
00:10:39.787 --> 00:10:41.947
from lesson eight with a sixth part,

377
00:10:41.947 --> 00:10:42.487
verification.

378
00:10:42.487 --> 00:10:43.687
So

379
00:10:44.227 --> 00:10:45.467
you have goal,

380
00:10:45.467 --> 00:10:47.687
inputs, output, limits,

381
00:10:47.687 --> 00:10:49.647
verification, and stop,

382
00:10:49.647 --> 00:10:51.027
one sentence each.

383
00:10:51.027 --> 00:10:53.587
The authorization from module one fits inside

384
00:10:53.587 --> 00:10:55.827
it: goal and stop stay,

385
00:10:55.827 --> 00:10:56.567
files become inputs,

386
00:10:56.567 --> 00:10:59.347
actions and time become limits.

387
00:10:59.347 --> 00:11:01.060
Denise filled in the six fields in

388
00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:03.340
four minutes, for the draft minutes of

389
00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.380
the teaching staff meeting,

390
00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:05.540
based on the agenda.

391
00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.120
They're fields of a work order,

392
00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.460
not magic words.

393
00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:12.180
Write the minutes leaves open the format,

394
00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.680
the length, and what to do about

395
00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:14.580
what's missing.

396
00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:16.780
Look at what happened when Denise asked

397
00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:17.880
for good minutes,

398
00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:19.840
with only the agenda pasted in.

399
00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:21.240
She got minutes of a meeting held

400
00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.380
on March twelfth,

401
00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:23.640
at two in the afternoon,

402
00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:24.760
in

403
00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:26.080
the teachers' lounge.

404
00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.320
Date, time, and place weren't in the

405
00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.640
agenda: the AI filled them in with

406
00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:31.900
a guess.

407
00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:33.340
With the six fields,

408
00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.680
the answer changed.

409
00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:35.980
She got one line per item,

410
00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.080
with Lúcia on the science fair calendar

411
00:11:38.080 --> 00:11:40.440
and Marcos on math tutoring.

412
00:11:40.440 --> 00:11:42.820
The date was marked as not informed,

413
00:11:42.820 --> 00:11:44.880
and so was the third item,

414
00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:46.480
which had no one responsible in the

415
00:11:46.480 --> 00:11:47.240
agenda.

416
00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:48.100
At the end,

417
00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:49.360
the verification:

418
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.000
the three items and the two people

419
00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:52.620
responsible are in the minutes,

420
00:11:52.620 --> 00:11:53.760
and

421
00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:54.860
nothing was sent.

422
00:11:54.860 --> 00:11:56.960
The contract settled the format,

423
00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:58.440
the length, and what's missing,

424
00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.420
and

425
00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:00.840
the AI stopped guessing.

426
00:12:01.140 --> 00:12:02.140
Good,

427
00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:04.860
clear, and complete are wishes,

428
00:12:04.860 --> 00:12:06.800
and nobody can check a wish.

429
00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:09.540
Verification uses criteria that anyone can check

430
00:12:09.540 --> 00:12:11.000
by looking at the result,

431
00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:13.140
like the quality ruler from lesson four.

432
00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.180
Lúcia used to ask for well-explained experiment

433
00:12:15.180 --> 00:12:16.320
procedures.

434
00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.300
She swapped that for two criteria:

435
00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.580
each step starts with a verb,

436
00:12:20.580 --> 00:12:22.520
and every material mentioned in the steps

437
00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.880
is on the materials list.

438
00:12:24.880 --> 00:12:27.000
Now she checks each procedure in a

439
00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:27.740
minute.

440
00:12:27.740 --> 00:12:29.120
And the easier it is to check,

441
00:12:29.120 --> 00:12:30.700
the sooner a slip shows up.

442
00:12:30.700 --> 00:12:32.040
In Denise's minutes,

443
00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:34.920
the verification said two people responsible.

444
00:12:34.920 --> 00:12:36.320
She counted in the agenda and in

445
00:12:36.320 --> 00:12:37.620
the minutes, two and two,

446
00:12:37.620 --> 00:12:38.900
in thirty seconds,

447
00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:40.680
because the

448
00:12:40.680 --> 00:12:42.160
minutes were a list.

449
00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:43.840
Pause the video and fill in a

450
00:12:43.840 --> 00:12:47.020
contract with a made-up five-item agenda,

451
00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.780
no real names.

452
00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.180
Send it in the chat,

453
00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:53.040
check one criterion directly against the agenda,

454
00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:54.640
and save the answer for the next

455
00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:55.540
lesson.

456
00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.460
The AI said it's done.

457
00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:58.160
Is it really done?

458
00:12:58.160 --> 00:13:00.240
The word done doesn't show that the

459
00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:02.240
file opens, or that the data was

460
00:13:02.240 --> 00:13:03.440
kept.

461
00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.620
A small check,

462
00:13:04.620 --> 00:13:05.320
done by you,

463
00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:07.901
usually finds more problems than asking again

464
00:13:07.901 --> 00:13:09.701
to make it better.

465
00:13:09.701 --> 00:13:11.561
It's like checking your grocery bag against

466
00:13:11.561 --> 00:13:13.381
the receipt before you leave.

467
00:13:13.381 --> 00:13:14.521
It's not enough for the bag to

468
00:13:14.521 --> 00:13:16.581
be full: every item on the receipt

469
00:13:16.581 --> 00:13:17.321
has to be there,

470
00:13:17.321 --> 00:13:19.401
and nothing extra.

471
00:13:19.561 --> 00:13:20.901
Lúcia got the minutes from the science

472
00:13:20.901 --> 00:13:23.601
department meeting and compared each decision with

473
00:13:23.601 --> 00:13:24.601
the agenda.

474
00:13:24.601 --> 00:13:25.781
For the lab schedule,

475
00:13:25.781 --> 00:13:27.561
the person responsible was herself,

476
00:13:27.561 --> 00:13:29.281
same as the agenda.

477
00:13:29.281 --> 00:13:30.141
For buying reagents,

478
00:13:30.141 --> 00:13:32.421
the agenda said not defined,

479
00:13:32.521 --> 00:13:34.661
and the minutes had someone named Paulo.

480
00:13:34.661 --> 00:13:35.761
A made-up name,

481
00:13:35.761 --> 00:13:37.421
found in two minutes of comparing.

482
00:13:37.421 --> 00:13:39.321
The minutes looked complete.

483
00:13:39.321 --> 00:13:42.361
Only the line-by-line comparison showed the error.

484
00:13:42.461 --> 00:13:44.281
You don't need to reread everything.

485
00:13:44.281 --> 00:13:45.281
Pick three points.

486
00:13:45.281 --> 00:13:48.041
A fact, that matches the source.

487
00:13:48.041 --> 00:13:50.001
A format, that's what you asked for.

488
00:13:50.001 --> 00:13:51.161
And an action,

489
00:13:51.161 --> 00:13:53.561
that works or was done the way

490
00:13:53.561 --> 00:13:54.541
you agreed.

491
00:13:54.541 --> 00:13:56.061
In the attendance report,

492
00:13:56.061 --> 00:13:58.291
Denise checked whether the total absences for

493
00:13:58.291 --> 00:14:00.141
seventh grade A matched the sum in

494
00:14:00.141 --> 00:14:02.341
the spreadsheet, whether the file opened with

495
00:14:02.341 --> 00:14:03.501
one column per month,

496
00:14:03.501 --> 00:14:05.221
and whether the spreadsheet link,

497
00:14:05.221 --> 00:14:06.401
mentioned in the report,

498
00:14:06.401 --> 00:14:06.901
opened.

499
00:14:06.821 --> 00:14:08.901
It's also worth asking the AI for

500
00:14:08.901 --> 00:14:09.661
evidence.

501
00:14:09.661 --> 00:14:12.163
I reviewed everything and it's correct doesn't

502
00:14:12.163 --> 00:14:13.763
say what was reviewed.

503
00:14:13.763 --> 00:14:15.043
Ask it to show what it checked,

504
00:14:15.043 --> 00:14:16.523
side by side with the source,

505
00:14:16.523 --> 00:14:18.603
and to say what it didn't check.

506
00:14:18.603 --> 00:14:20.323
A test that was run isn't a

507
00:14:20.323 --> 00:14:22.343
test that was suggested.

508
00:14:22.343 --> 00:14:24.243
And even the AI's I checked

509
00:14:24.243 --> 00:14:25.383
it is a claim:

510
00:14:25.383 --> 00:14:27.623
spot-check one item on the list.

511
00:14:27.623 --> 00:14:28.523
Finally,

512
00:14:28.523 --> 00:14:30.103
write down what you observed in each

513
00:14:30.103 --> 00:14:32.223
check, with the exact result.

514
00:14:32.223 --> 00:14:33.283
Found an error?

515
00:14:33.283 --> 00:14:35.723
Fix the request too before

516
00:14:35.903 --> 00:14:36.703
you reuse it,

517
00:14:36.703 --> 00:14:38.023
or the source,

518
00:14:38.023 --> 00:14:40.503
if the error came from there.

519
00:14:40.503 --> 00:14:43.563
Otherwise, the error comes back next time.

520
00:14:43.563 --> 00:14:45.863
Lúcia corrected the name

521
00:14:46.043 --> 00:14:48.083
in the minutes and added a line

522
00:14:48.083 --> 00:14:49.963
to the delivery contract:

523
00:14:49.983 --> 00:14:52.283
anyone responsible that the agenda doesn't define

524
00:14:52.283 --> 00:14:54.523
becomes not informed.

525
00:14:54.523 --> 00:14:56.403
And if you don't find any error

526
00:14:56.403 --> 00:14:57.843
at all,

527
00:14:58.003 --> 00:14:58.803
that's a great sign:

528
00:14:58.803 --> 00:15:01.063
write down what you compared it with,

529
00:15:01.063 --> 00:15:03.223
because the log shows you looked,

530
00:15:03.223 --> 00:15:04.943
not just that you trusted it.

531
00:15:04.943 --> 00:15:06.263
Pause the video now.

532
00:15:06.263 --> 00:15:08.333
Take the delivery you saved in lesson

533
00:15:08.333 --> 00:15:09.783
eleven, or

534
00:15:09.843 --> 00:15:12.343
the practice agenda and minutes from this

535
00:15:12.343 --> 00:15:13.123
lesson.

536
00:15:13.123 --> 00:15:14.203
Check a fact,

537
00:15:14.203 --> 00:15:15.464
a format, and an action,

538
00:15:15.464 --> 00:15:17.984
like something sent without permission,

539
00:15:17.984 --> 00:15:20.024
and write three notes with the result

540
00:15:20.024 --> 00:15:20.704
of each.

541
00:15:20.704 --> 00:15:22.964
Let's put it all together.

542
00:15:23.584 --> 00:15:24.744
For a small question,

543
00:15:24.744 --> 00:15:26.044
the chat is enough,

544
00:15:26.044 --> 00:15:27.964
as long as you say who it's

545
00:15:27.964 --> 00:15:29.084
for and what it's for,

546
00:15:29.084 --> 00:15:31.324
and ask for the assumptions.

547
00:15:31.324 --> 00:15:32.944
For a bigger task,

548
00:15:32.944 --> 00:15:35.164
you write a work order with goal,

549
00:15:35.164 --> 00:15:37.164
inputs, output, limits,

550
00:15:37.164 --> 00:15:38.264
and stop.

551
00:15:38.264 --> 00:15:39.324
Before the work,

552
00:15:39.324 --> 00:15:41.564
you confirm what the AI read,

553
00:15:41.864 --> 00:15:44.404
with the name and the first and

554
00:15:44.404 --> 00:15:45.104
last line.

555
00:15:45.104 --> 00:15:47.084
You know where the task runs,

556
00:15:47.084 --> 00:15:48.404
reads, and saves,

557
00:15:48.404 --> 00:15:50.464
and whatever you don't know becomes a

558
00:15:50.464 --> 00:15:51.284
pending item.

559
00:15:51.284 --> 00:15:53.404
You bring it all together in a

560
00:15:53.404 --> 00:15:56.464
delivery contract, with a verification someone else

561
00:15:56.464 --> 00:15:56.984
can check.

562
00:15:56.984 --> 00:15:59.264
And you only call it done after

563
00:15:59.264 --> 00:16:00.404
checking a fact,

564
00:16:00.404 --> 00:16:02.164
a format, and an action.

565
00:16:02.164 --> 00:16:04.144
When you have about thirty minutes,

566
00:16:04.144 --> 00:16:06.424
do the module's optional lab,

567
00:16:06.484 --> 00:16:07.844
From loose question to work order,

568
00:16:07.844 --> 00:16:10.624
in the additional material for lesson twelve.

569
00:16:10.624 --> 00:16:11.804
In module three,

570
00:16:11.804 --> 00:16:14.204
terminal and Codex in practice.

571
00:16:14.204 --> 00:16:15.644
The delivery contract comes along,

572
00:16:15.644 --> 00:16:16.664
now

573
00:16:16.664 --> 00:16:19.064
with an AI that works in a

574
00:16:19.064 --> 00:16:20.664
folder of yours.

575
00:16:20.764 --> 00:16:21.447
See you there.
